WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.252 --> 00:00:01.477
- When I first started rapping,

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:03.884
I just wanted to make $2,000 a month.

00:00:03.884 --> 00:00:06.408
People that's big or that
you perceive to be big,

00:00:06.408 --> 00:00:07.580
they're not big, they're just big

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.378
because they treat
themselves like they're big.

00:00:09.378 --> 00:00:10.707
- I wasn't going to be a doctor.

00:00:10.707 --> 00:00:11.540
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.424
- You know, I wasn't going to be a lawyer.

00:00:13.424 --> 00:00:14.655
I wasn't going to be,

00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:16.079
you know, I didn't see myself

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:17.526
putting on a suit or tie every day.

00:00:17.526 --> 00:00:18.359
- Mmmhmm.

00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:20.802
- He's an American
rapper from Los Angeles.

00:00:20.802 --> 00:00:24.530
Since 2008, he has released
five independent mix tapes.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.755
He is known for his laid back flow,

00:00:26.755 --> 00:00:28.903
wordplay, and unique storytelling.

00:00:28.903 --> 00:00:31.096
He's Dom Kennedy, and here's my take on

00:00:31.096 --> 00:00:32.844
his Top 10 Rules for Success.

00:00:32.844 --> 00:00:34.753
Rule number three is my personal favorite,

00:00:34.753 --> 00:00:37.279
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:37.279 --> 00:00:38.580
And as always, as you're watching,

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.820
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.364
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:42.364 --> 00:00:43.580
put quotes around it,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.543
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:45.543 --> 00:00:47.601
And when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.416
to stick with you, as well.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.249
Enjoy.

00:00:52.605 --> 00:00:56.105
(lively, inspiring music)

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.599
- What I try to do is, always,

00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:07.294
you know, better myself.

00:01:07.294 --> 00:01:08.127
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:08.127 --> 00:01:11.325
As a person, as just a
human being on God's Earth,

00:01:11.325 --> 00:01:13.332
or what you want to call it.

00:01:13.332 --> 00:01:16.394
I feel like, focusing on too much today.

00:01:16.394 --> 00:01:17.799
Kids focus on,

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:20.178
and even a lot of my
friends, the end result,

00:01:20.178 --> 00:01:22.264
which is the money, you know, the fame,

00:01:22.264 --> 00:01:23.097
and all of that side.

00:01:23.097 --> 00:01:25.991
But it's like, if you don't
learn anything about yourself,

00:01:25.991 --> 00:01:28.076
if you don't take anybody with you,

00:01:28.076 --> 00:01:28.909
you know what I'm saying,

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:31.093
if you don't change anybody's
life for the better,

00:01:31.093 --> 00:01:32.348
and you do it alone.

00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:34.464
It's not going to mean nothing.

00:01:34.464 --> 00:01:35.990
You're going to end up
somewhere by yourself

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.954
unhappy about it, anyway.

00:01:37.954 --> 00:01:38.965
- [Interviewer] That's
right, that's right.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.703
- So that's kind of like
what I tell my friends

00:01:40.703 --> 00:01:41.556
and how I try to live my life.

00:01:41.556 --> 00:01:43.939
- [Female Interviewer] Was
there ever a point that you were

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:45.313
so close to quitting?

00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:46.897
- Yeah, it was.

00:01:46.897 --> 00:01:47.730
I wouldn't say,

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.674
I couldn't say like, so close.

00:01:49.674 --> 00:01:51.512
I don't know how close, you know?

00:01:51.512 --> 00:01:52.345
- Mmmhmm.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.055
- But it was definitely a
time where I was just like,

00:01:54.055 --> 00:01:58.222
you know, I didn't have a lot
expectations, like I said.

00:02:01.011 --> 00:02:03.474
I got to a point where I
had done a lot of things.

00:02:03.474 --> 00:02:04.578
I had kind of passed.

00:02:04.578 --> 00:02:05.411
When I first started rapping,

00:02:05.411 --> 00:02:07.803
I just wanted to make $2000 a month.

00:02:07.803 --> 00:02:08.636
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:02:08.636 --> 00:02:09.469
- That's why I honestly tell my friends--

00:02:09.469 --> 00:02:10.302
- You said a month?

00:02:10.302 --> 00:02:11.135
I heard that.

00:02:11.135 --> 00:02:12.743
- Like man, if I could
figure out a way to make

00:02:12.743 --> 00:02:14.720
$2,000 a month,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.859
you know, I would be happy.

00:02:16.859 --> 00:02:17.812
- You're almost there, huh.

00:02:17.812 --> 00:02:18.794
- Yeah, man.

00:02:18.794 --> 00:02:20.053
It's getting close.
- Keep grinding, man

00:02:20.053 --> 00:02:22.013
$24,000 a year, brother, it's coming.

00:02:22.013 --> 00:02:22.846
- Exactly.

00:02:22.846 --> 00:02:23.692
- (laughs)

00:02:23.692 --> 00:02:27.859
- So, at a certain point, I
put out music, I traveled,

00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:31.327
and it was just like,
yeah, I was questioning.

00:02:31.327 --> 00:02:33.070
You know you have to
find a reason every day

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.980
to want to still do something,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.025
so, I kind of had to re-focus,

00:02:37.025 --> 00:02:38.294
but yeah, it was, though.

00:02:38.294 --> 00:02:40.111
Man, take yourself serious.

00:02:40.111 --> 00:02:43.074
You know, don't wait on
nobody else to validate you.

00:02:43.074 --> 00:02:45.193
Take yourself serious,
you know what I'm saying,

00:02:45.193 --> 00:02:46.679
'cause people only going mess with you

00:02:46.679 --> 00:02:48.104
as serious as you take yourself.

00:02:48.104 --> 00:02:49.737
So if you think you the small time,

00:02:49.737 --> 00:02:52.432
everybody going to think you small time.

00:02:52.432 --> 00:02:53.527
Nobody ain't going to have no reason to.

00:02:53.527 --> 00:02:54.543
People that's big,

00:02:54.543 --> 00:02:56.136
or that you perceive to be big,

00:02:56.136 --> 00:02:57.112
they're not big.

00:02:57.112 --> 00:02:57.945
They're just big because

00:02:57.945 --> 00:02:59.516
they treat themselves like they're big.

00:02:59.516 --> 00:03:02.095
You know what I'm sayin',
they act important.

00:03:02.095 --> 00:03:03.635
They're important people to themselves.

00:03:03.635 --> 00:03:05.446
So the world has to take you as such,

00:03:05.446 --> 00:03:08.215
because, you know, that's who you are.

00:03:08.215 --> 00:03:09.819
Most important lessons I learned was just,

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:11.624
man, don't be scared to take a chance,

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.259
you know, on yourself.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.730
Nothing is guaranteed.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.058
There's nothing that
you're ever going to do

00:03:16.058 --> 00:03:17.701
where you're going to
know exactly, for sure,

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:20.267
that the outcome is
going to be successful,

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:22.398
but you got to go anyway.

00:03:22.398 --> 00:03:23.231
You got to protect yourself,

00:03:23.231 --> 00:03:25.775
and the only way you can
do that is by working hard.

00:03:25.775 --> 00:03:27.124
You know, to guarantee that the outcome

00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:29.707
will be one that you will like.

00:03:31.952 --> 00:03:32.893
It takes a while to get to that point,

00:03:32.893 --> 00:03:34.778
where it's like, you're okay with

00:03:34.778 --> 00:03:38.013
putting music out and
putting out albums and stuff.

00:03:38.013 --> 00:03:40.179
But I like to do it until I feel like

00:03:40.179 --> 00:03:42.083
I've given enough to that project.

00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:44.555
And then when I'm at that
place, and I'm satisfied,

00:03:44.555 --> 00:03:45.938
and I feel like no matter the outcome,

00:03:45.938 --> 00:03:47.040
I'm happy with it,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.982
that's when it comes out.

00:03:48.982 --> 00:03:51.783
- I was reading an
article on you on Forbes,

00:03:51.783 --> 00:03:53.097
which is amazing.

00:03:53.097 --> 00:03:54.606
Because for you to be on Forbes

00:03:54.606 --> 00:03:56.145
they were really studying

00:03:56.145 --> 00:03:57.783
your work as an independent artist,

00:03:57.783 --> 00:03:59.400
and kind of like how you are in a position

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.136
where you can tell a label,
"This is what I want,"

00:04:02.136 --> 00:04:04.091
and then tell them, "Nah, I'm
not going to take that deal,"

00:04:04.091 --> 00:04:05.911
because I already got my movement.

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.248
Tell me about how you got to that place,

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.992
because obviously that
didn't happen overnight.

00:04:09.992 --> 00:04:12.421
- Nah, it happened gradually,

00:04:12.421 --> 00:04:14.148
you know, out of necessity, really.

00:04:14.148 --> 00:04:16.537
You know, it started with me

00:04:16.537 --> 00:04:18.419
just being a fan of music, first of all.

00:04:18.419 --> 00:04:20.186
I say that, like, I wasn't--

00:04:20.186 --> 00:04:22.489
When I was a kid and when I was younger,

00:04:22.489 --> 00:04:24.464
you know, in my early 20's,

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:27.651
you feel me, I wasn't
really meant to be a rapper.

00:04:27.651 --> 00:04:28.484
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:28.484 --> 00:04:30.173
I always wrote.

00:04:30.173 --> 00:04:32.653
Like, I feel like a lot of kids
in the inner city can rhyme.

00:04:32.653 --> 00:04:34.168
You know what I'm saying,
and they love rap,

00:04:34.168 --> 00:04:35.502
and they buy albums.

00:04:35.502 --> 00:04:39.901
But then as I start putting
out music and learning more,

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:42.826
it kind of just prepared me for this.

00:04:42.826 --> 00:04:44.367
So every project I did,

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.612
every failure I had,

00:04:45.612 --> 00:04:46.685
it made me smarter.

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:47.690
It made me stronger.

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:49.785
You know, every time I slipped,

00:04:49.785 --> 00:04:51.584
right after I slipped, I got up.

00:04:51.584 --> 00:04:53.822
You know what I'm sayin',
and it just kept going,

00:04:53.822 --> 00:04:54.872
it just kept building.

00:04:54.872 --> 00:04:56.950
Fill a void. You know?

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:58.887
Fill a void. It's jobs out here.

00:04:58.887 --> 00:05:01.263
Figure out what you can make better.

00:05:01.263 --> 00:05:02.732
That's better than any job.

00:05:02.732 --> 00:05:04.847
Like, you could go get
a job doing something,

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:06.380
whatever you want to, but figure out

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.000
where you can really fit in and be happy.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.005
And then worry about, the
money's going to come.

00:05:11.005 --> 00:05:12.062
That's not going to be a problem.

00:05:12.062 --> 00:05:13.559
Because if you're filling a void,

00:05:13.559 --> 00:05:15.748
and you're adding to, you know, whatever,

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.735
you might be like, "You know what?

00:05:17.735 --> 00:05:20.080
They don't have good food at venues."

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.024
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:21.024 --> 00:05:22.578
And you might be the person,

00:05:22.578 --> 00:05:26.591
the next billionaire that just
have bomb food at concerts.

00:05:26.591 --> 00:05:27.561
Like straight up, though.

00:05:27.561 --> 00:05:28.394
- [Interviewer] Yeah, that's true.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:29.429
- Straight up, though,
or just figure out a way

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:32.137
to involve, like, media in concerts.

00:05:32.137 --> 00:05:33.966
Like where people could be there and

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.949
you could like, you know,
whatever, some type of way.

00:05:35.949 --> 00:05:38.728
But just figure out something
that people is not doing.

00:05:38.728 --> 00:05:40.925
You know what I'm saying,
that you feel like

00:05:40.925 --> 00:05:44.036
people could utilize and do that.

00:05:44.036 --> 00:05:47.703
- What's your sort of
definition of success?

00:05:48.788 --> 00:05:51.642
- You know, for me, it's
just peace and happiness.

00:05:51.642 --> 00:05:54.311
You feel me, that was the
last song on the yellow album.

00:05:54.311 --> 00:05:56.949
You know, and that was really
the message that I learned

00:05:56.949 --> 00:05:59.863
in all that time, and
all my time doing music.

00:05:59.863 --> 00:06:01.936
Up to that point, for
me, that was success.

00:06:01.936 --> 00:06:03.103
You know, peace and happiness.

00:06:03.103 --> 00:06:07.451
And for me, happiness
is just giving my all,

00:06:07.451 --> 00:06:09.296
you know, to whatever
I'm doing at the time.

00:06:09.296 --> 00:06:11.456
Again, it's not, you know.

00:06:11.456 --> 00:06:12.289
Like, I haven't--

00:06:12.289 --> 00:06:13.515
I've only sold two projects.

00:06:13.515 --> 00:06:15.209
Like, that was my biggest project today,

00:06:15.209 --> 00:06:16.910
and I gave it away for free.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.466
You know, so it wasn't really,

00:06:19.466 --> 00:06:20.514
I had to see if I,

00:06:20.514 --> 00:06:22.420
you know, prove it to myself, like,

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:23.532
I would do this for free,

00:06:23.532 --> 00:06:26.164
so I would definitely would
do it for money, obviously.

00:06:26.164 --> 00:06:28.341
But it's not really for that.

00:06:28.341 --> 00:06:30.451
You know, it's for something else, for me.

00:06:30.451 --> 00:06:32.786
And it was definitely at that time,

00:06:32.786 --> 00:06:35.605
and it was just to be
dedicated to something,

00:06:35.605 --> 00:06:37.640
for your life to have a purpose.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.390
I decided around 2005

00:06:40.372 --> 00:06:43.885
that I wanted to be, you
know, an entertainer.

00:06:43.885 --> 00:06:44.718
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:06:44.718 --> 00:06:47.775
- And rap was something I
had already been involved in.

00:06:47.775 --> 00:06:51.117
You know, just as a childhood,
it was a passion of mine.

00:06:51.117 --> 00:06:53.164
So I figured it was my best,

00:06:53.164 --> 00:06:55.997
you know, route to take
applying everything I know,

00:06:55.997 --> 00:06:57.012
everything I had.

00:06:57.012 --> 00:06:58.943
Like, I wasn't going to be a doctor.

00:06:58.943 --> 00:06:59.776
- Okay.

00:06:59.776 --> 00:07:01.684
- You know, I wasn't going to be a lawyer.

00:07:01.684 --> 00:07:02.780
I wasn't going to be,

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:04.011
you know, I didn't see myself

00:07:04.011 --> 00:07:06.173
putting on a suit or tie everyday.

00:07:06.173 --> 00:07:07.271
I'm just being honest.

00:07:07.271 --> 00:07:09.334
So I, you know, you kind of look down

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:11.542
the list of, like, what's
your possibilities.

00:07:11.542 --> 00:07:13.042
You know, what are you going to do?

00:07:13.042 --> 00:07:16.971
So, it's kind of like we
chose each other, I guess.

00:07:16.971 --> 00:07:18.464
You know with any project,

00:07:18.464 --> 00:07:19.890
you kind of hope it would.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.857
The Yellow Album was little step

00:07:21.857 --> 00:07:23.373
further than what I normally do,

00:07:23.373 --> 00:07:24.618
you know, musically.

00:07:24.618 --> 00:07:27.852
And I had, it was a
very ambitious project.

00:07:27.852 --> 00:07:30.333
You know, and there was
times when I was making it

00:07:30.333 --> 00:07:31.877
that I didn't really know.

00:07:31.877 --> 00:07:34.127
You know, but that's the fun
part about being an artist,

00:07:34.127 --> 00:07:36.544
you know, is to challenge yourself.

00:07:36.544 --> 00:07:38.675
You know, I think that's why
it's been my best project.

00:07:38.675 --> 00:07:40.361
So, I worked really hard on it.

00:07:40.361 --> 00:07:42.836
There was a lot of nights, I was like,

00:07:42.836 --> 00:07:45.494
you know, sat up and yawned,
listen to songs like,

00:07:45.494 --> 00:07:46.905
"Man I wonder what
people are going to think

00:07:46.905 --> 00:07:48.646
or if they going to even like this."

00:07:48.646 --> 00:07:50.860
But, you know, I'm more than happy with

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.435
how it turned out, for sure.

00:07:52.435 --> 00:07:54.998
Like, I get inspired by life a lot,

00:07:54.998 --> 00:07:58.084
and that's my way of
giving back and expressing.

00:07:58.084 --> 00:08:01.138
And people, you know, I get
inspired by people basically,

00:08:01.138 --> 00:08:02.888
and that's my way of,

00:08:04.435 --> 00:08:05.936
of showing that, is music.

00:08:05.936 --> 00:08:08.606
So, the only way that I can do that is,

00:08:08.606 --> 00:08:12.791
the only way I do that is with rap songs.

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:13.952
As soon as I find a beat,

00:08:13.952 --> 00:08:15.702
or music that I love,

00:08:16.589 --> 00:08:17.422
I can get to you.

00:08:17.422 --> 00:08:18.754
You know what I mean?

00:08:18.754 --> 00:08:19.587
Giving back.

00:08:19.587 --> 00:08:21.809
So, it's like I sit around,

00:08:21.809 --> 00:08:23.461
I go to the studios.

00:08:23.461 --> 00:08:24.808
I wait for those moments

00:08:24.808 --> 00:08:26.972
to hear music that I love,

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:30.143
that I could write something
that I never written before.

00:08:30.143 --> 00:08:31.659
And make a song I feel like

00:08:31.659 --> 00:08:33.318
the world has never heard it before.

00:08:33.318 --> 00:08:35.103
Kids, you know, from my area,

00:08:35.103 --> 00:08:37.247
and people, like, they
have never heard before.

00:08:37.247 --> 00:08:40.597
Just inspire them to
do something different,

00:08:40.597 --> 00:08:43.061
and be themselves even more, you know?

00:08:43.061 --> 00:08:44.765
Like, if you listen to my music,

00:08:44.765 --> 00:08:46.649
you know, it varies from time to time,

00:08:46.649 --> 00:08:48.316
but it kind of stays

00:08:49.277 --> 00:08:51.517
the same in terms of uniqueness.

00:08:51.517 --> 00:08:52.965
I would think so.

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:56.215
You know, like, I just look for unique.

00:08:58.797 --> 00:09:01.171
I don't want to say professional legit.

00:09:01.171 --> 00:09:03.073
You know what I mean, it
sound like a real person

00:09:03.073 --> 00:09:06.323
that really knows what
they're doing, mainly.

00:09:06.323 --> 00:09:07.944
I don't like to--

00:09:07.944 --> 00:09:09.420
you know, I don't know.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.648
There are different levels of,

00:09:10.648 --> 00:09:12.982
you know, musicianship,

00:09:12.982 --> 00:09:16.984
but the people that I tend
to work with are more like,

00:09:16.984 --> 00:09:17.968
you know, like how I am.

00:09:17.968 --> 00:09:19.242
They're sure about what,

00:09:19.242 --> 00:09:20.773
like, when I'm sure when I write a song,

00:09:20.773 --> 00:09:21.880
or when I'm Don Kennedy,

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:22.980
or when I hit the stage,

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.822
like, I know what I'm going to do.

00:09:24.822 --> 00:09:26.262
You know, so I look for producers

00:09:26.262 --> 00:09:29.108
that have that same
confidence in what they do.

00:09:29.108 --> 00:09:30.237
You know, and is not
worried about trying to do

00:09:30.237 --> 00:09:32.088
what everybody's trying to do.

00:09:32.088 --> 00:09:35.266
And just have their own thing
that they bring to the table.

00:09:35.266 --> 00:09:37.183
That's what I look for.

00:09:39.411 --> 00:09:40.818
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:40.818 --> 00:09:43.608
I made this video because
Mikey Linan asked me to.

00:09:43.608 --> 00:09:44.766
Also, if you want to nominate someone

00:09:44.766 --> 00:09:46.405
for the next top ten video,

00:09:46.405 --> 00:09:48.743
please check the description
for a link to a video

00:09:48.743 --> 00:09:50.473
where you could vote for people,

00:09:50.473 --> 00:09:52.084
and put in your suggestions as well.

00:09:52.084 --> 00:09:54.508
I'd love to know what did
you take from this video.

00:09:54.508 --> 00:09:57.573
What was the most important
lesson that you learned,

00:09:57.573 --> 00:09:58.650
that blew your mind,

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:00.672
that you're going to immediately apply

00:10:00.672 --> 00:10:02.705
to your life or your business somehow.

00:10:02.705 --> 00:10:04.423
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:10:04.423 --> 00:10:05.786
I'm super curious to find out.

00:10:05.786 --> 00:10:07.809
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Clyde Hayz.

00:10:07.809 --> 00:10:09.154
Clyde, thank you so much for

00:10:09.154 --> 00:10:11.384
picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word.

00:10:11.384 --> 00:10:12.217
Taking that picture

00:10:12.217 --> 00:10:13.569
and posting it on Instagram.

00:10:13.569 --> 00:10:15.259
I love the effects you put on it.

00:10:15.259 --> 00:10:16.647
I really appreciate the support

00:10:16.647 --> 00:10:18.127
and I hope you're enjoying the book.

00:10:18.127 --> 00:10:19.873
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:10:19.873 --> 00:10:21.215
I believe in you.

00:10:21.215 --> 00:10:23.090
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:25.273
and whatever your One Word is.

00:10:25.273 --> 00:10:26.472
Much love.

00:10:26.472 --> 00:10:27.972
I'll see you soon.

00:10:33.854 --> 00:10:36.159
- I can't tell no man, or no kid, nobody,

00:10:36.159 --> 00:10:38.075
that you should try your best in school,

00:10:38.075 --> 00:10:40.162
if I'm not trying my
best at what I'm doing.

00:10:40.162 --> 00:10:40.995
- Yeah.

00:10:40.995 --> 00:10:41.828
- You know what I'm
saying, they going to know,

00:10:41.828 --> 00:10:44.219
they're going to be like,
"Man, you just getting over it.

00:10:44.219 --> 00:10:45.894
I just want to be like you."

00:10:45.894 --> 00:10:47.464
But it's like, no, I'm
not getting over it, dog.

00:10:47.464 --> 00:10:48.736
I don't go to sleep.

00:10:48.736 --> 00:10:49.569
- Yeah.

00:10:49.569 --> 00:10:50.903
- You know what I'm saying?

00:10:50.903 --> 00:10:53.664
Like, I be up stressin' nights, working,

00:10:53.664 --> 00:10:56.618
trying to figure out perfect
ways to express myself

00:10:56.618 --> 00:10:58.846
and, you know, come up
with t-shirt designs.

00:10:58.846 --> 00:11:02.212
Like, this is something
I do 'cause I love it.

00:11:02.212 --> 00:11:03.045
You know what I'm sayin', and

00:11:03.045 --> 00:11:04.693
I love and I work hard at it,

00:11:04.693 --> 00:11:07.356
and it rewards me for being loyal to it.

00:11:07.356 --> 00:11:08.832
You know, not the other way around.

00:11:08.832 --> 00:11:11.289
Like, you don't just get
paid because you show up.

00:11:11.289 --> 00:11:13.426
- So I know after you
released the other album,

00:11:13.426 --> 00:11:15.625
you sort of, toured
the world and all that,

00:11:15.625 --> 00:11:16.789
sort of, for the first time.

00:11:16.789 --> 00:11:19.506
How did those kind of
experiences affect you,

00:11:19.506 --> 00:11:21.256
and sort of, affect--

00:11:22.912 --> 00:11:23.963
- First of all,

00:11:23.963 --> 00:11:27.269
it showed me just,
really the power in just,

00:11:27.269 --> 00:11:29.810
you know, believing in yourself.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:31.467
'Cause me making the Yellow Album,

00:11:31.467 --> 00:11:33.802
you know, it wasn't a risk at all.

00:11:33.802 --> 00:11:35.854
It was a calculated risk, if anything.

00:11:35.854 --> 00:11:38.409
But it showed the power of me, to me,

00:11:38.409 --> 00:11:42.576
of believing in yourself
and believing in your art.

